#!/bin/bash

################################################################################
#                                                                              #
# Script to download corpora from the Linguistic Data Consortium               #
#                                                                              #
# Original author: Lane Schwartz                                               #
# Additional contributors: None                                                #
#                                                                              #
#                                                                              #
# Change log:                                                                  #
#                                                                              #
#  * 2026-08-14                                                                #
#    Run without a terminal, so the script can be driven by automation.        #
#      - Read LDC_EMAIL / LDC_PASSWORD / LDC_DOWNLOAD_DIR from the environment #
#        or from ldc.env (beside this script) or ~/.ldc.env. Still prompts     #
#        when stdin is a terminal and nothing was configured.                  #
#      - Exit instead of silently posting empty credentials when there is no   #
#        terminal to prompt on, and check that login actually succeeded.       #
#      - Reuse the session in cookies.txt rather than logging in every run.    #
#      - Download every part of a multi-part corpus. A corpus is all catalog   #
#        rows whose ID matches exactly, deduplicated by (filename, MD5);       #
#        previously a multi-row corpus produced a malformed URL.               #
#      - Keep each file's real extension instead of assuming .tgz.             #
#      - Verify by MD5, or by exact byte count when the catalog still lists    #
#        the checksum as "calculating".                                        #
#      - Write to <name>.part and rename only after verifying, resume          #
#        interrupted transfers, and skip files that are already correct.       #
#      - Keep the password out of ps by passing it to curl from a file.        #
#      - Fix the timestamp format (%M is minutes; the month is %m).            #
#                                                                              #
#  * 2016-03-05 Lane Schwartz                                                  #
#    Verify that downloaded files are tgz, not HTML.                           #
#    If HTML, exit the script, because file was not correctly downloaded       #
#                                                                              #
#  * 2016-03-05 Lane Schwartz                                                  #
#    Download a richer set of information into the corpora.tsv file            #
#    and record that information in the names of the downloaded files          #
#                                                                              #
#  * Created on 2016-03-04 by Lane Schwartz                                    #
#    Based on Python code by Jonathan May:   https://github.com/jonmay/ldcdl   #
#                                                                              #
